    "semantic_notes": [
      {
        "heading": "[ edit 6 2 Quick Notes ]",
        "text": "Dror likes to call 6_2 \"The Miller Institute Knot\", as it is the logo of the Miller Institute for Basic Research . The bowline knot of practical knot tying deforms to 6_2 . It looks like the crabber's eye knot of practical knot tying deforms to 6_2 also, although the bowline and crabber's eye knot are considered different knots in practical knot tying, given how they are tied, and insofar as how they carry load differently based upon that. [ edit 6 2 Further Notes and Views ] The Miller Institute Mug [1] Simple square depiction 3D depiction",
        "source": "rendered-text-window"
      },
